        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ipqu1m3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Oxidation and Reduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3q8j11q",
      "content": "Oxidation: Addition of oxygen or loss of hydrogen."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Oxidation",
        "Reduction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Oxygen Transfer",
          "Gain of Oxygen",
          "Loss of Oxygen"
        ],
        [
          "Hydrogen Transfer",
          "Loss of Hydrogen",
          "Gain of Hydrogen"
        ],
        [
          "Electron Transfer",
          "Loss of Electrons (LEO)",
          "Gain of Electrons (GER)"
        ],
        [
          "Oxidation State",
          "Increase in Oxidation Number",
          "Decrease in Oxidation Number"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "r50mfoe"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "81wlw6f",
      "content": "Reduction: Removal of oxygen or gain of hydrogen."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nhq6izd",
      "content": "These reactions together are called redox reactions."
    },
    {
      "id": "qyvol7l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Exothermic and Endothermic Reactions"
    },
    {
      "id": "2p9r6ya",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Reaction Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Exothermic Reaction</p>",
            "<p>Releases heat energy</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Endothermic Reaction</p>",
            "<p>Absorbs heat energy</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1zohaxw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Corrosion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9mjh0o1",
      "content": "Corrosion is the gradual destruction of metals due to chemical reactions with the environment. Rusting of iron is the most common example."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v89ah4n",
      "content": "Example of rusting:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txenqko",
      "content": "Iron + Oxygen + Water → Rust"
    },
    {
      "id": "1tgy3sh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Rancidity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wdr429z",
      "content": "Rancidity refers to the oxidation of fats and oils in food which causes unpleasant smell and taste. It can be prevented by storing food in airtight containers."
    },
    {
      "id": "zlpo4un",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Catalysts"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Respiration is an exothermic process, whereas photosynthesis and thermal decomposition are endothermic processes.",
        "Electrolysis of water produces hydrogen gas at the cathode and oxygen gas at the anode in a 2:1 volume ratio.",
        "Galvanization protects iron from rusting by coating it with a thin layer of protective zinc metal.",
        "Nitrogen gas is used to flush food items packaged with oils and fats to prevent spoilage via rancidity."
      ],
      "id": "8pfivjw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mqkc2cv",
      "content": "A catalyst is a substance that increases the rate of a chemical reaction without being consumed in the reaction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "631waer",
      "content": "Examples: Platinum, Iron catalyst in Haber process"
    },
    {
      "id": "ke4sxbh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d8tgcut",
      "content": "• Chemical equations represent chemical reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "culvq0s",
      "content": "• Rusting of iron is a common example of corrosion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "11prqcr",
      "content": "• Redox reactions involve oxidation and reduction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nmocg53",
      "content": "• Exothermic reactions release heat energy."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}